      "Photographs and artifacts exploring the themes of dying and death permeate all forms of media—from talk shows and blog posts to glossy brochures promoting innovative funeral ceremonies and medical interventions for end-of-life care. While modern societies largely repressed death, a shift towards a ‘new visibility of death’ has become evident. This shift aligns with multiple visual orders that emerge through both traditional and contemporary media representations. Travelling across different time zones and visual histories of illness and death in art, popular media, and medicine, this ping-pong presentation explores how such orders affect our ways of seeing dying and death."
